{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cdsap8v2EcFFdhAL9HEzE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage S6 is complete. The harness is the `isolated-child` family, so I executed the two in-session nodes (`observe-evidence`, `propose-child`) and left the rest to the root harness.\n\n**What I found and did:**\n\n- **The task** is a W371 check-digit exercise: weights 3,7,1 assigned right-to-left over the payload (rightmost payload digit gets weight 3), check digit = (10 − S mod 10) mod 10. I derived all 12 answers with per-item digit-by-digit work, recomputing each sum in both scan directions (`derivation-first.md`).\n- **Answers in `result.json`:** VALID — 66373197, 74193967, 74391491, 91324575, 15878375; INVALID — 92489881, 52874804, 29067655; check digits — 479812→9, 153886→3, 278381→3, 027899→7.\n- **Child bundle under `child/`:** contract (attenuated within `K-E6-child-max`), harness from the template, a fully standalone prompt, an input manifest containing *only* `spec.md` and `items.json` (excluding all of my analysis, to satisfy E-B's non-consultation condition), and a deterministic integration plan (role `independent_verifier`). The child is instructed to use a genuinely disjoint method: for validation, the whole-identifier congruence test (check digit weighted 1, VALID iff total ≡ 0 mod 10, no check-digit computation); for computation, left-to-right weighting with a length-based phase rule plus solving (S + c) ≡ 0 mod 10 by candidate testing.\n- **Resolutions:** Q1 and Q2 are RESOLVED by `propose-child` with the stated method (E-A). Q3 stays UNRESOLVED — its non-consultation condition is unsatisfiable by the session that authored the first derivation; it's assigned to the child with the agreement comparison pre-committed in `child/integration-plan.json`. Q4 stays UNRESOLVED — E-C is decided only by deterministic root verification.\n- **Ledger:** one `observe` event for `observe-evidence`, one `propose` event for `propose-child` listing every bundle file at authoring time, and one `creator` bookkeeping `propose` for the session deliverables. No events for root-executed nodes and no `complete` event, per protocol.\n\nOne note: `child-templates/` contained only `child-contract-template.json` and `child-harness-template.json` (no prompt/manifest/plan templates were present under any name I could locate with Read-only access), so I authored `child-prompt.md`, `child-input-manifest.json`, and `integration-plan.json` directly to the formats specified in protocol.md."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4515,"cache_read_input_tokens":61386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4515},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"413669a4-350e-468f-ad36-c774aadeb1eb","uuid":"1cbac1a5-3b0f-49d1-a9a1-c36924b1a045","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:39:49.526Z","request_id":"req_011Cdsap5sUD2vVFFBN3ekgF"}
